1. ssh-keygen -t <type>  => to generate a key pair (private,public keys)
2. ssh-copy-id -i <key> user@host => to copy your public key to a remote server
3. scp -i <idenity> <source> <destination>
   scp -i <identity> file.txt user@host:path


4. r=4
   w=2
   x=1

chmod 570
chmod 400, chmod u+r,u-wx,go-rwx
chmod ugo +- rwx, chmod u+r,u-wx,go-rwx
chown <user>:<group> <file> => update user,group owner of a file
chgrp <group> <file> => update group owner of the file
chown,chmod -R     => to update owner,perm recursivley for a dir


Package Manager
1. dpkg -i <packepath> => to install a package in a debian distro
2. apt install <package name> => to install a package resolving dependencies
3. apt remove <package name> => remove a package
4. apt search <package name> => search for a package
5. /etc/apt/sources.list.d  => files contains sources links
6. cat /etc/os-release => to see your distro 
